WEBVTT

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.670
Hey, there...

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.590
Want a walnut?

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.010
This is really starting to get interesting!

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:50.820
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.480
Always go

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.900
On my own

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.120
Always go

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.750
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:17.140
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:23.220
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:32.150
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.650
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:45.330
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:51.380
All we have left is the future

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:57.800
Please become our reason to continue living

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:04.470
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.230
Morning.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.280
Did you get any sleep?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.550
The Rainbow of Albion

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.220
Good morning, Commander.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.300
Good morning.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.480
Now, then...

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.860
I've requested approval from headquarters for subjects under observation and protection

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.940
on this base to wear these.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.240
The time has come for us to rectify mistakes of the past.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.540
Why are you freeing him?

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.250
I'm rectifying our mistakes.
I've cleared this with HQ.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.210
Use of lead gears on this base is now forbidden!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:23.930
Globe's internal observation agency—Salty Dog—will not allow this.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.720
I'm the one in charge here!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.560
The commander's so cool.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.860
My opinion of him just improved.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.120
A-Akari...

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.790
What are you doing here?

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.000
What am I doing here?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.540
Allow me to introduce you.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.630
This is Yomatsuri Akari.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.510
That's the commander's daughter...

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.880
She went with his wife after they split, you know.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.090
Isn't his wife, Governor Yomatsuri, aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i>?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.550
Hi there, everyone.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.520
I'm magical girl Akari!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.560
Magical girl?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.690
You're the girl from yesterday?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.610
Yes, she is Code Papillon,

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.270
last night's flight director.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.320
What the hell is going on?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.650
She is also an extremely talented hacker.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.860
She has at several points attempted to hack <i>Alonzo</i>.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.620
We can't afford to not have her here.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.370
I've been planning to have her cooperate with us for a while now.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.500
Akari's a hacker?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.540
A magical girl!

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.540
H-Hey...

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.500
Wait!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:36.830
Don't touch that!

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.380
Oh, God...

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.300
How could he be so cruel to a daughter he hasn't seen in five years?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.300
He hasn't seen her in five years.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.680
My opinion of him just dropped.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.140
How did li'l ol' me end up a magical girl?

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.100
"Li'l ol' me"?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.190
Is she a bumpkin?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.730
My father is the commander of Globe's Tanegashima base.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.150
And my mother is governor of the satellite base <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.200
My parents, concerned only with their jobs, abandoned me,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.990
and left me so very lonely.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.870
My computer was my only friend...

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.700
I know the truth!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.000
Four years ago, I was so excited

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:21.000
that my father was going to spend my birthday with me for once!

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.380
And the reason for his last-second cancellation was...

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:27.430
that he actually had a date with Miss Rita right there!

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.890
No, y-you see...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:32.470
We needed to secure her recruitment to this base as soon as possible...

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.230
I'm sorry...

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.600
Pathetic, Commander.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.810
My opinion of him just plummeted.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.410
Annou

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.410
Yams

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.410
Annou Yams?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.080
Delicious!

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.040
I'm sorry, both of you...

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.800
For what?

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.800
Keeping you locked in the base for all this time.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.010
I truly am sorry.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.640
Will you allow me to recruit her?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.690
By the way, I don't come cheap.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.270
Very well.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:25.780
However, she'll live with me, along with the three others.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.530
Do you mean Teppei and Hana?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:33.080
And Daichi, as well?

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.910
That's right.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.660
I should have done this sooner...

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:44.500
I'm so grateful that Daichi made me realize it.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.850
The wind on this island feels good, doesn't it?

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.180
Yeah, it does.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.690
Hey...

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.020
Is this you?

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.230
Ah... Yup.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.780
My dad and Uncle Nishikubo were good friends.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.530
So when I was little, I used to stay here a lot.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.080
I loved this island...

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.790
That's you, isn't it?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.630
Hey, I'm back.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.550
You can actually cook!

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.720
I can't make anything too complicated.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.430
Looks pretty good, doesn't it?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.550
Yeah.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:34.970
It smells great.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.640
You're cuter when you smile.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.270
Listen up...

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.400
From now on, you're family, and this is your house.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.740
But you're growing boys and girls living beneath the same roof.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.860
So try to show some restraint.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.410
You know what I'm talking about, right?

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.080
Restraint?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:57.950
Restraint?

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.330
Was the cologne in the bathroom a present from Miss Rita?

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.920
Don't worry about small things like that!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.880
It makes you a small person.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.130
Um...

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.800
I can't find the switch for the steam bath...

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.300
We don't have one here!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.510
My restraint!

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.560
Restraint...

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.140
She has me beat...

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.560
She's totally in the lead now.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.980
I love the way this house smells!

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.780
It smells old.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:32.070
But it's got heart.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.950
Welcome back.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:38.700
So this is a friend of yours!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.290
Did you like the walnut?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.670
You know Pitz?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.750
I saw him at the shrine today.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.500
The shrine?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.250
On this island, there's an old shrine.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.010
And there's a legend about it...

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.970
Long ago, a messenger descended from heaven and left behind a huge rock

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.310
with an angel sealed inside.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:04.850
Hey...

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.650
Which do you think is a stronger heroine, a magical girl or an angel?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.070
There are so many stars, I can't find the Big Dipper.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.620
This island has barely any streetlamps.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.950
It really is amazing...

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.000
The Milky Way?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.830
Well, the Milky Way is amazing too, but...

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.250
Just two days ago, I was wondering what I should be doing with my life...

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.670
It's all amazing.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.470
It's thanks to that rainbow you showed me.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.970
That round rainbow... I always thought it was something I'd imagined as a kid.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.020
Hey, Daichi...

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.320
Doesn't it creep you out?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.200
What?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.490
You haven't changed.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.660
You always surprise me.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.870
Your Livlaster really surprised me.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.580
So...

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.380
This is yours.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.300
Okay, the game's back on!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:21.760
No!

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.930
I cannot allow Manatsu Daichi to participate in any further missions.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.730
Even if the Globe Federation

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.110
has decided unanimously?

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.250
Doghouse to Pointer.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.880
The fact that this Manatsu Daichi boy defeated

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.920
the Kill-T-Gang with his Livlaster is having a significant effect.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:03.640
That said, Impactors other than the Earth Engine are also capable of that.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:08.230
Globe is currently investigating the use of low-orbit Impactors, as well.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.980
I think eliminating them at close range in the stratosphere is likely to be the more reliable way.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.860
But doesn't that risk damaging the planet's surface too much?

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:15.690
Over.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.320
We're past the point where considerations like that may still be taken.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.660
Mutou Hana is absolutely necessary to the Kivotos Plan.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.490
Do not forget that

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:27.160
having her under our control is a top priority for those of us in the Ark Faction.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:31.620
Thus, it will be up to you to deal with Manatsu Daichi.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.590
Manatsu Daichi...

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:45.010
Monetizing the basic theory behind the Machine Goodfellows and the Designer's Children alone

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.180
would make a lot of people wealthy.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.810
And CEO Kube gets everything...

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:57.780
But it was an artificial intelligence named Pac that
developed the basic theory, don't you remember?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.820
He's got it pretty good.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:00.440
Hey!

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.150
I'm afraid I can't overlook this.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.950
Oh, I mean, uh...

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.580
Your secretary, little Hitomi,

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:13.290
is totally in love with you.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.580
Why don't you make her yours?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.300
Have there been any more Kill-T-Gang attacks?

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.430
I've heard that manned Impactor is supposed to be called the Earth Engine.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.720
I kicked its ass last time.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.680
If it was powered by a Livlaster,

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:33.600
does that mean they can use the Princess of <i>Blume</i> now?

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.940
Have fun tonight.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.220
Approaching-Earth Object has been sighted!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:10.810
It's a Kill-T-Gang!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:17.650
The world hasn't seen the real me in nine long years.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:20.270
I may have underestimated the Earthlings last time, but...

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.240
That's...

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.740
The Type-1 that killed Manatsu Daichi's father.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.990
I can use this...

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.710
A Kill-T-Gang has been sighted within Defensive Zone 1, Alpha sector!

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.840
It's path will intersect with Earth in

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.090
34,000 kilometers!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.170
Its approach speed is 52 kilometers per second!

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:50.760
They want me to write a report about when I got the Livlaster, but I don't know what to say...

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.230
Howdy.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.610
Was there something you needed?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.200
That is so very cold of you, Manatsu Daichi.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:14.080
It seems that a certain Kill-T-Gang has returned.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.170
And would you like to hear something interesting?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.000
It really is...

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.840
the same type that appeared nine years ago!

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.440
No, it's the very same model!

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:42.610
Commander,

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.780
Alonzo has approved an emergency launch of the Earth Engine!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.190
They're launching the Pegasus rocket!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.680
The Earth Engine is generating propulsion!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.510
What's going on?!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.770
I explicitly prohibited that!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.310
And I have sanctioned it.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.610
Governor, the expansion sequence has been activated again!

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.730
What did you say?!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.740
Manatsu Daichi has already proven that he can defend the Earth.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:37.200
That Kill-T-Gang that is currently approaching Earth

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.830
is the same one that killed your father nine years ago.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.150
Commander!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.910
You're launching the Earth Engine?! Are you insane?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:02.620
None of its post-combat maintenance—beyond replacing its armor—has been completed!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.330
Ah, that might be a bit of a problem.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:15.510
But, should the need arise,
we have low-orbit Impactors.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.010
You've overstepped yourself!

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:17.800
Leave this area!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:23.430
As of now, Salty Dog is to be denied access to the control room and all other secured blocks!

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.230
And thus Manatsu Daichi comes to an end.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:46.580
What's wrong?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.210
Come with me!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.510
Commander! Alpha Sector's Impactors are not responding!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:54.970
This is awful...

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.430
The relay satellite that forwards planetary commands isn't responding.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.680
Maybe if I try bouncing it off another satellite...

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:01.390
Akari!

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.770
Leave it to the magical girl!

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:04.980
Logical, logical...

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:08.560
German Impactors, you are now mine to command!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.860
"Logical"? That's not magic...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.860
Impactor Feigen's interception systems are coming on line!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.780
Akari's doing this?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.160
She's gained control of the German Impactors?

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:29.120
This is nothing compared to the Thousand System I cracked open a while back.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:30.830
Wait a second...

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:35.920
You were behind those American Air Force hackings last year?

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.920
Don't worry about small things like that.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.340
It makes you a small person.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.720
You've got to be kidding...

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:51.310
A dream, an echo singing of pleasant memories

00:18:51.690 --> 00:19:01.280
It glows like that promise I'm sure we made

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.190
An earthquake?

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.820
Tanegashima is the epicenter!

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:24.390
It reaches the lonely depths of my soul

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:22.050
I won't underestimate you this time!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.010
Impactor Feigen has been lost!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.930
The Earth Engine is entering the Kill-T-Gang's effective range!

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:34.360
It's reminding me of a wait somewhere someday

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.020
Do you hear me, Daichi?

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:29.430
The Earth Engine hasn't been repaired since you were in it!

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.440
Turn back immediately!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.020
Hey, Uncle...

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:43.820
The future blooms in front of my eyes

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.360
My dad flew to stop that thing, didn't he?

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:44.030
Then that means I have to stop it.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:48.120
So I set off to seek you

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:45.620
Otherwise,

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.120
what my dad did will be meaningless!

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:53.750
To say our goodbyes

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:52.620
I won't let you go any further!

00:19:53.750 --> 00:20:03.390
A dream, a love blooming like the sun in the sky

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.760
It's reacting so sluggishly...

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.180
It hasn't been repaired at all!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:13.440
It's the light of a day when it was my turn to do the protecting

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:16.360
My fangs will tear you apart, Earth Engine!

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:31.710
It's telling me that I lost nothing

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.570
What's that?

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.030
A planetary sign?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:41.550
Because the smile on your face never fades

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:36.380
Albion!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:50.220
Please, my dear future, don't cry

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.680
What?

00:20:51.020 --> 00:21:01.230
Our paths may meet again someday

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:56.650
Albion... What are you doing?!

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:10.870
A dream, an echo singing of pleasant memories

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:19.840
It glows like that promise I'm sure we made

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:24.670
It gently strokes my cheek

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.010
That Kill-T-Gang...

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.260
It's a friend.

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:29.600
Like sunlight through the trees

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.260
Hana?

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:39.730
And I tie it all into a bouquet meant for you

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.600
It's a friend.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.450
Teppei, is that you?

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:04.920
Are you okay, Teppei?

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:06.550
Yes.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:10.760
This thing's main system never worked before.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:13.060
Why has it turned on now?

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:17.940
That earthquake was <i>Blume</i> moving.

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:21.360
It was you, wasn't it?

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.940
I just sang.

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:27.400
Either way...

00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:32.450
Maybe it's thanks to God that we survived today.

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:35.500
God?

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:41.330
I can't say I've ever met this "God".

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:55.020
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:55.020 --> 00:23:00.560
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:05.400
aren't always good things

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:13.070
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:22.540
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:30.680
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:36.720
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:42.600
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:45.650
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:53.820
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:57.240
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.240 --> 00:24:03.380
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:16.970
Teppei was able to pilot an enemy robot.

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:18.640
What does that mean?

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:22.640
Globe's Tanegashima base is split over Teppei's true identity.

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:26.520
And then, two of the enemy launch a bold assault!

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:30.440
Next time, on episode 4 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:32.990
Assault of the Planetary Gear.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:32.990
Assault of the Planetary Gear

00:24:33.610 --> 00:24:36.320
Earth Engine, expand!
